{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01EXnmYqcE4pac7Jr37nK1T8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FTm264KYGoctC3pD3NFYmj","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/sysoper/workspace/WhileISleep/batch-output/tesseract-ocr-image-processor/README.md","old_string":"## Getting Started\nTBD — fill in once prototype is scaffolded.","new_string":"## Getting Started\n\n**Requirements:** `tesseract-ocr`, `tesseract-ocr-eng` (or other language pack), `ghostscript`\n\n```bash\n# Basic usage — processes all PNG/JPG/TIFF in input_dir\n./ocr.sh input_dir output_dir\n\n# With a different language\n./ocr.sh input_dir output_dir --lang fra\n```\n\nPer image, three files are written to `output_dir` (mirroring the input subdirectory structure):\n- `<name>.txt` — plain-text transcript\n- `<name>.hocr` — hOCR with word bounding boxes\n- `<name>.pdf` — searchable PDF with embedded invisible text layer\n\nA run log is written to `output_dir/ocr.log`. The script exits non-zero if any image fails.\n\n**Word-highlight viewer:** Open `hocr-viewer.html` in a browser, select the original image and the corresponding `.hocr` file, then click \"Render highlights\" to see yellow boxes over each recognised word.\n\n## To Do\n\n- [ ] Add `--skip-existing` flag for resume mode (skip images whose output files already exist)\n- [ ] Verify multi-page TIFF behaviour (tesseract handles them natively; output naming differs)\n- [ ] Add `--output-formats` flag to selectively produce txt/hocr/pdf subsets\n- [ ] Optionally copy original images alongside output for self-contained viewer bundles"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378,"cache_read_input_tokens":33419,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":378},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a9a0c21-250b-47df-bfb8-035bd6b27178","uuid":"f5d5696f-a26d-4ff0-b065-1a1188a9def3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FTm264KYGoctC3pD3NFYmj","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/sysoper/workspace/WhileISleep/batch-output/tesseract-ocr-image-processor/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a9a0c21-250b-47df-bfb8-035bd6b27178","uuid":"6655947c-0a35-4a51-8f63-b187afc28e6f","timestamp":"2026-04-23T04:19:42.271Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/sysoper/workspace/WhileISleep/batch-output/tesseract-ocr-image-processor/README.md","oldString":"## Getting Started\nTBD — fill in once prototype is scaffolded.","newString":"## Getting Started\n\n**Requirements:** `tesseract-ocr`, `tesseract-ocr-eng` (or other language pack), `ghostscript`\n\n```bash\n# Basic usage — processes all PNG/JPG/TIFF in input_dir\n./ocr.sh input_dir output_dir\n\n# With a different language\n./ocr.sh input_dir output_dir --lang fra\n```\n\nPer image, three files are written to `output_dir` (mirroring the input subdirectory structure):\n- `<name>.txt` — plain-text transcript\n- `<name>.hocr` — hOCR with word bounding boxes\n- `<name>.pdf` — searchable PDF with embedded invisible text layer\n\nA run log is written to `output_dir/ocr.log`. The script exits non-zero if any image fails.\n\n**Word-highlight viewer:** Open `hocr-viewer.html` in a browser, select the original image and the corresponding `.hocr` file, then click \"Render highlights\" to see yellow boxes over each recognised word.\n\n## To Do\n\n- [ ] Add `--skip-existing` flag for resume mode (skip images whose output files already exist)\n- [ ] Verify multi-page TIFF behaviour (tesseract handles them natively; output naming differs)\n- [ ] Add `--output-formats` flag to selectively produce txt/hocr/pdf subsets\n- [ ] Optionally copy original images alongside output for self-contained viewer bundles","originalFile":"# Tesseract OCR Image Processor\n\n## Goal\nProvide a Bash script that runs Tesseract OCR over images in an input directory and produces output files (text + hOCR/PDF overlay) in a separate output directory, preserving word-position data for highlight-capable viewing.\n\n## Scope\n- **In scope:** Batch processing of common image formats (PNG, JPG, TIFF), output of `.txt` and `.hocr` (or searchable PDF) per image, output to a configurable destination folder\n- **In scope:** hOCR output enables word highlighting in compatible viewers (e.g., browser-rendered hOCR or PDF with text layer)\n- **Out of scope:** Building a custom viewer — the hOCR/PDF output relies on existing tools (browser, `evince`, `okular`)\n- **Out of scope:** Training custom Tesseract models\n\n## Getting Started\nTBD — fill in once prototype is scaffolded.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":4,"newStart":10,"newLines":29,"lines":[" - **Out of scope:** Training custom Tesseract models"," "," ## Getting Started","-TBD — fill in once prototype is scaffolded.","+","+**Requirements:** `tesseract-ocr`, `tesseract-ocr-eng` (or other language pack), `ghostscript`","+","+```bash","+# Basic usage — processes all PNG/JPG/TIFF in input_dir","+./ocr.sh input_dir output_dir","+","+# With a different language","+./ocr.sh input_dir output_dir --lang fra","+```","+","+Per image, three files are written to `output_dir` (mirroring the input subdirectory structure):","+- `<name>.txt` — plain-text transcript","+- `<name>.hocr` — hOCR with word bounding boxes","+- `<name>.pdf` — searchable PDF with embedded invisible text layer","+","+A run log is written to `output_dir/ocr.log`. The script exits non-zero if any image fails.","+","+**Word-highlight viewer:** Open `hocr-viewer.html` in a browser, select the original image and the corresponding `.hocr` file, then click \"Render highlights\" to see yellow boxes over each recognised word.","+","+## To Do","+","+- [ ] Add `--skip-existing` flag for resume mode (skip images whose output files already exist)","+- [ ] Verify multi-page TIFF behaviour (tesseract handles them natively; output naming differs)","+- [ ] Add `--output-formats` flag to selectively produce txt/hocr/pdf subsets","+- [ ] Optionally copy original images alongside output for self-contained viewer bundles"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0112rrhweAWhSSE6dYZ8i5sR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Prototype is complete and verified. Here's what was built:\n\n- **`ocr.sh`** — batch Tesseract wrapper: finds all PNG/JPG/TIFF under `<input_dir>`, runs `tesseract ... txt hocr pdf` per file, mirrors subdirectory structure in `<output_dir>`, logs every success/failure to `ocr.log`, exits non-zero on any failure. Uses `readonly` config vars, `set -euo pipefail`, no silent error swallowing.\n- **`hocr-viewer.html`** — single-file browser viewer: load an image + its `.hocr` file, click Render, yellow boxes appear over each recognised word (scaled to the rendered image size).\n- **`Dockerfile` / `.dockerignore`** — `debian:12-slim` base, installs `tesseract-ocr-eng` + `imagemagick` + `ghostscript`, generates two test images at build time (one in a subdirectory), CMD runs the full script.\n\nDocker run confirmed: OCR correctly read `\"Hello World OCR Test\"` and `\"Subdirectory image batch test\"`, subdirectory mirroring worked, all `.txt`/`.hocr`/`.pdf` triples were produced."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":572,"cache_read_input_tokens":33797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":572},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a9a0c21-250b-47df-bfb8-035bd6b27178","uuid":"5cff2aea-4afa-4abb-8c35-d714ae7f2d71"}
